# Build outputs -- every CMake/ninja build directory in this project is
# named "build" at the project root of whatever it's building. Regenerate
# with cmake+ninja; never commit compiled objects/binaries.
build/
native/*/build/
native/*/*/build/

# Python virtual environments for the ML child-process runtime (DAC/
# EnCodec/MT3 scoping -- see STATUS.md's "Twenty-third"/"Twenty-fourth"
# sections) -- gigabytes of installed packages and downloaded model
# weight caches, never source. Python's own `venv` module auto-writes a
# `.gitignore` (containing `*`) inside each venv it creates, which
# already excludes most of these -- but that's inconsistent across
# Python launchers (confirmed directly: a venv created via an
# Astral-managed Python distribution did NOT get one, and would have
# been swept into a broad `git add` untracked-and-unnoticed). This
# explicit rule doesn't rely on that per-venv file existing.
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/*_env/

# Downloaded pretrained model weight caches (DAC/EnCodec cache under the
# venvs' own torch hub dir, already covered above; MR-MT3's checkpoint
# cache -- mt3-infer's own download location -- is a sibling directory,
# not inside a venv, so needs its own rule). ~175MB for MR-MT3 alone;
# re-downloaded automatically on first real use, never committed.
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/.mt3_checkpoints/

# Scratch test-fixture output from this session's own smoke testing
# (synthetic input/output audio and MIDI, log dumps) -- not source, freely
# regenerated by re-running native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/
# smoke_test_*.py.
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/*smoke_input.wav
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/*smoke_output.*
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/*smoke_output_log.txt
native/BeatShoreDesktop/python_engine/mt3_tail.txt

# Vendored third-party SDKs -- large (JUCE ~117MB, VST3 SDK ~500MB) and
# not this project's own code. Fetch these separately per each SDK's own
# distribution instructions rather than committing them; see each
# directory's own README/CMakeLists.txt for the pinned version this
# project builds against (JUCE 9.0.1, VST3 SDK 3.8.1 -- see STATUS.md).
native/JUCE/
native/vst3sdk/

# Node dependencies -- reinstall via `npm ci --omit=dev` (see
# native/installer/build-release.ps1 -CleanEngine, or STATUS.md's
# "Installer size" section for the exact trim applied to production
# installs). Never commit node_modules.
node_modules/
native/BeatShoreDesktop/engine/node_modules/

# Downloaded build tooling -- the pinned standalone Node 24 toolchain
# used by build-release.ps1 for -CleanEngine. Re-download from
# nodejs.org rather than committing a ~106MB binary redistribution.
native/installer/tools/

# Installer staging and output -- entirely regenerated by
# native/installer/build-release.ps1 on every run; committing these
# would mean committing a copy of the trimmed node_modules tree, staged
# binaries, and every compiled installer .exe.
native/installer/stage/
native/installer/Output/
native/installer/staging-file-hashes.txt
native/installer/release-report.json

# Editor/OS noise
.vs/
*.user
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code session state -- this machine/session's own lock file
# (PID, process start time, session id), not project source.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# One-off setup byproducts from cloning the vendored SDKs (see the JUCE/
# vst3sdk exclusion above) -- not source, not needed once those SDKs are
# actually present.
native/juce-clone.log
native/vst3sdk-clone.log
